<section class="mv-hero"><div class="mv-w mv-hero-g"><div class="mv-hero-t"><p class="mv-k">Fit &amp; fabric, decoded</p><h1>Clothes feel better when they <em>fit</em> and the fabric is right.</h1><p class="mv-lead">Modevia is an independent fashion guide about the two things that decide how clothes look and last: fit and fabric. Convert sizes, choose fabrics for the weather and plan your seasonal wardrobe.</p><p class="mv-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Open the tools</a><a class="mv-ln" href="fabric-guide.html">Read the fabric guide</a></p></div>
<div class="mv-orbs"><figure class="mv-o1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794849658327-7d70e775997b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=460&q=75" alt="woman with long dark hair in a black top" width="460" height="460" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="mv-o2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794556386030-8158af711fa4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="man in a brown turtleneck and dark jacket" width="300" height="300" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="mv-o3"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794881037543-e116fb25353e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=260&h=260&q=75" alt="woman in sunglasses and beige trousers sitting on rocks" width="260" height="260" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="mv-marq" aria-label="Topics"><div class="mv-w"><span>Linen</span><span>Merino</span><span>Cotton poplin</span><span>Denim</span><span>Shoulder seams</span><span>Rise</span><span>Inseam</span><span>Drape</span></div></section>

<section class="mv-s"><div class="mv-w mv-two"><div><p class="mv-k">The basics</p><h2>Fit first, then fabric, then style</h2><p class="mv-lead">A well-fitting plain shirt beats an expensive one that pulls across the back. Get these three things right before anything else.</p></div><ol class="mv-trio"><li><b>01</b><div><h3>Shoulders</h3><p>Hardest to alter, so they must fit off the rack. Seams sit on the edge of the shoulder bone.</p></div></li><li><b>02</b><div><h3>Length</h3><p>Sleeves end at the wrist bone, trousers just touch the shoe, jackets cover the seat.</p></div></li><li><b>03</b><div><h3>Fabric weight</h3><p>Heavier fabrics drape and hide lines; lighter ones breathe and move.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="mv-tl" id="tools"><div class="mv-w"><p class="mv-k">Style tools</p><h2>Three tools, one tap each</h2><div class="mv-acc">
<details open><summary><span>i.</span>Clothing Size Converter<small>US &middot; UK &middot; EU &middot; letter</small></summary><div class="mv-acc-b"><div class="mv-f"><label for="sc-g">Clothing<select id="sc-g"><option value="w">Women&rsquo;s tops &amp; dresses</option><option value="m">Men&rsquo;s shirts (collar)</option></select></label><label for="sc-s">Size system<select id="sc-s"><option value="us">US</option><option value="uk">UK</option><option value="eu">EU</option></select></label><label for="sc-v">Your size<input id="sc-v" type="number" step="1" value="8"></label></div><div class="mv-out" id="sc-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></details>
<details><summary><span>ii.</span>Fabric Finder<small>season &middot; feel &middot; care</small></summary><div class="mv-acc-b"><div class="mv-f"><label for="ff-s">Season<select id="ff-s"><option value="hot">Hot summer</option><option value="mild" selected>Spring or autumn</option><option value="cold">Winter</option></select></label><label for="ff-f">You want it to feel<select id="ff-f"><option value="crisp">Crisp and structured</option><option value="soft" selected>Soft and easy</option><option value="stretch">Stretchy and active</option></select></label><label for="ff-c">Care you&rsquo;ll accept<select id="ff-c"><option value="easy">Machine wash only</option><option value="any">Happy to hand wash or iron</option></select></label></div><div class="mv-out" id="ff-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></details>
<details><summary><span>iii.</span>Season Switch Planner<small>what to store, what to bring out</small></summary><div class="mv-acc-b"><div class="mv-f"><label for="ss-n">Moving into<select id="ss-n"><option value="summer">Summer</option><option value="autumn" selected>Autumn</option><option value="winter">Winter</option><option value="spring">Spring</option></select></label><label for="ss-r">Wardrobe space<select id="ss-r"><option value="small">Small: one rail</option><option value="mid" selected>Medium</option><option value="large">Large</option></select></label></div><div class="mv-out" id="ss-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></details>
</div></div></section>

<section class="mv-s"><div class="mv-w mv-look"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794505949499-3a5e6ef38ddd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=660&q=75" alt="person buttoning a purple and white striped shirt" width="560" height="660" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="mv-k">Read the label</p><h2>What a care label tells you</h2><dl class="mv-lab"><div><dt>Fibre content</dt><dd>Percentages of each fibre. Over 2&ndash;3% elastane means noticeable stretch.</dd></div><div><dt>Wash symbol</dt><dd>The tub with a number is the maximum temperature in &deg;C.</dd></div><div><dt>Iron symbol</dt><dd>One dot is cool, two is warm, three is hot.</dd></div><div><dt>Circle</dt><dd>Professional cleaning only. Ignore it at your fabric&rsquo;s risk.</dd></div><div><dt>Square</dt><dd>Drying instructions; a circle inside means tumble dry.</dd></div></dl></div></div></section>

<section class="mv-dark"><div class="mv-w mv-dark-g"><blockquote>&ldquo;Buy for the body you have today, and have it tailored to fit perfectly.&rdquo;</blockquote><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794905522307-a6a3f6222730?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=380&q=75" alt="two women in fashion with large ruffled collars" width="560" height="380" loading="lazy"></div></section>

<section class="mv-s"><div class="mv-w"><p class="mv-k">Guides</p><h2>Read in depth</h2><div class="mv-gds"><a href="fabric-guide.html"><div class="mv-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793588410983-a3cd18d8f7ee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="white shirt with an embroidered hummingbird" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><div><span>Guide one</span><h3>The Fabric Guide</h3><p>Cotton, linen, wool, silk and modern blends: how each feels, wears and should be washed.</p></div></a><a href="fit-guide.html"><div class="mv-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794554748769-5acbb0b050f2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="man in a black trench coat and orange sweater" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><div><span>Guide two</span><h3>The Fit Guide</h3><p>How shirts, trousers, jackets and dresses should fit, and which problems a tailor can fix.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="mv-s mv-sand"><div class="mv-w mv-fq"><div><p class="mv-k">FAQ</p><h2>Fit &amp; fabric questions</h2><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794849642982-758a73b36a78?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=520&q=75" alt="woman in a black sweater" width="460" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mv-faq"><details open><summary>Which fabrics are best in hot weather?</summary><p>Linen, cotton poplin, seersucker and lightweight wool all breathe well. Loose weaves let air move, and natural fibres absorb sweat better than most synthetics.</p></details><details><summary>Why do clothes from different brands fit differently?</summary><p>Every brand uses its own fit model and size chart. A medium in one label can be an inch or two bigger in another, so it is worth checking measurements rather than the size on the tag.</p></details><details><summary>How should a shirt fit across the shoulders?</summary><p>The shoulder seam should sit at the edge of your shoulder bone. If it falls down your arm the shirt is too big; if it sits on top of your shoulder it is too small.</p></details><details><summary>Is natural fibre always better than synthetic?</summary><p>Not always. Natural fibres usually breathe and age well, while synthetics add stretch, strength and quick drying. Blends often combine the best of both.</p></details><details><summary>How can I tell if a fabric is good quality?</summary><p>Hold it to the light to check the weave is dense and even, scrunch it to see how it recovers from creasing, and look at the seams: they should be straight and tightly stitched.</p></details><details><summary>When should I take clothes to a tailor?</summary><p>When the fit is right in the shoulders and chest but wrong in length or waist. Hemming, taking in a waist and shortening sleeves are simple, affordable changes.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="mv-nl"><div class="mv-w mv-nl-g"><h2>The Modevia Fold</h2><p>One fabric explained and one fit fix, every month.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@modevia.com?subject=The%20Modevia%20Fold&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></section>

